      "tags": [
        "vessel",
        "generation ship"
      ],
      "card": "One of the five Flotilla ships — with Palestine, Brasilia, Islamabad and Baghdad — that left Mercury in 2083 for the 61 Cygni A system: humanity's first manned interstellar colonisation effort. Each was a two-kilometre re-purposed in-system freighter carrying 960 passengers in reefersleep caskets and a crew of 150, driven by a lithium/antilithium reaction with separate antimatter reservoirs for acceleration and deceleration. The destination planet was named Journey's End and renamed Sky's Edge by the colonists. Only three of the five reached it, undone by external sabotage and internal scheming; the Santiago was one of them, and Schuyler 'Sky' Haussmann sailed aboard her. DATES ARE APPROXIMATE: 2083 is the official departure, but the official timeline says only that the Flotilla would not arrive before the twenty-third century, so 2300 stands for the LATEST possible arrival rather than a documented one. The ship's own fate after arrival is not modelled."
    }
