      "tags": [
        "character"
      ],
      "bio": "Schuyler 'Sky' Haussmann — a 'momio', a sleeper awakened from reefersleep, who sailed on the Santiago. He jettisoned reefersleep caskets so the Santiago would arrive first at Journey's End, and the colonists renamed the planet 'Sky's Edge' as a mockery. Crucified through a stand-in, he slept a century in reefersleep, and became the centre of the Church of Sky cult and its indoctrination virus. He re-emerged as the arms dealer Cahuella, then as 'Tanner Mirabel', then as 'H' — the man who killed and replaced the Mademoiselle, and who drew Nevil Clavain into the Resurgam evacuation. Immortal; his death date is not established. DATES ARE APPROXIMATE: the official timeline fixes the Flotilla's 2083 departure and says it would not arrive before the twenty-third century, so 2300 stands in for the latest possible arrival at Sky's Edge; 2517 is the year Tanner Mirabel reaches Chasm City, by which point the Mirabel/Reivich sequence has played out. He was certainly in Chasm City by 2524, when he recruited Ana Khouri into Shadowplay. The Flotilla years (2083-2300) are not modelled — there is no node for the Santiago."
    }
